  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe local P104 fusions in #2662 and its newer #2712 successor preserve rank mass, but their positive moment gains do not yet quantify an allowance for additional hosting charges. This adds an independently implemented, source-bound certificate for that missing cost implication.\n\n```text\nPR2586 literal word -> PR2662 -> PR2712\n       independently recounted frame ranks and profiles\n       exact rational gain / one-added-H1 comparison\n```\n\nAt the selected complex primitive saving, the gains relative to #2586 are **0.5273081047\u2026** and **0.5409352129\u2026** rank-one child units. One uncompensated H1 outweighs either local gain when caller width, role normalization and all other charges are fixed. Certified G=1 brackets are `[0.003182398581, 0.003182398582]` and `[0.003101949576, 0.003101949577]`.\n\nOnly `research/p104-fusion-cost-headroom/` is added. It includes exact source pins, three compressed literal words, retained notices, a written enclosure/monotonicity proof, receipt, controls and registered replay. Credit commdata2338/#2662, ywz65/#2586/#2712 and Nick Petalas/#2550, with the earlier lineage retained. The [canonical claim and handoff](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2619#discussioncomment-18955520) and [concurrent conditional consumer screen](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2619#discussioncomment-18955566) distinguish the scopes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** predecessor profile improvements were qualitative; extra child charges remained open.\n  **After:** exact enclosures establish the allowance, and also show both local comparisons afford three H1 children at the separate planning benchmark a=1/99.\n- `python3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-fusion-cost-headroom` passes on CPython 3.12.14: normal/optimized primary, six mathematical controls and six oracle/artifact test groups. Tests cover source/receipt corruption, Git-free read-only replay, recompression, output refusal and resource limits. Ruff diagnostics pass.\n- No predecessor Python is imported. Source words are authenticated against exact Git blobs and SHA256; the selected benchmark is bound through its selected record and assembly. Separate internal arithmetic review agrees; no independent human or formal proof review is claimed.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way. Isolated research package and opt-in bounded replay.\n\n**Blast Radius:** research.\n\nThis is a fixed-profile local budget, with no offsetting credits. Actual idle savings, sharing, changed consumers and changed profiles need a new bill. Native correctness, ownership, precision, the other 102 forward correction rows, all-size admission and a complete favorable supplier moment remain open. No selected-frontier or kappa change; no supplier cold-replay claim.\n",
